WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- Thank you.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:03.030
I had to dress up for you.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.000
- You look so good.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.434
- Your audience is gorgeous.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:07.824
- [Kelly] They're so
gorgeous and they're so fun.

00:00:07.824 --> 00:00:08.657
- So colorful, yes.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:11.010
- We like to run shiny here.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.202
So wait, meet Terry, have y'all ever met?

00:00:12.202 --> 00:00:13.110
- Yeah. We've never met. The first time.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:13.943
- [Terry] We just did.

00:00:13.943 --> 00:00:14.776
- Just met. Are you a sports ball fan?

00:00:14.776 --> 00:00:16.442
- That's a good look.

00:00:16.442 --> 00:00:17.483
- [Kelly] It looks so good, right?

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:18.316
- Yeah.

00:00:18.316 --> 00:00:19.262
If I lose 60 pounds, I'm wearing that.

00:00:19.262 --> 00:00:20.095
(audience laughs)
- [Kelly] You walked out.

00:00:20.095 --> 00:00:20.928
- I gotta come here more.

00:00:20.928 --> 00:00:21.761
(Brandon laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:00:21.761 --> 00:00:23.058
- You walked out here. I was like okay.

00:00:23.058 --> 00:00:23.967
(Brandon laughs)

00:00:23.967 --> 00:00:25.470
But wait, so you went to the Emmy's

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.090
for the first time this
year? I did as well.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:27.923
It was my first time.

00:00:27.923 --> 00:00:29.220
- I saw you. I know. We
didn't know each other.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.053
But I saw you.

00:00:30.053 --> 00:00:30.886
- Well, it was my first time too.

00:00:30.886 --> 00:00:32.100
I was a little nervous
'cause I'd never done that

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.300
and it was a long walk out there.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.133
- [Brandon] It's a very long walk.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.130
- Yeah, and did you have a good time?

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.330
- I had a wonderful time.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.240
So, I was there with my best
friend who's on Rings of Power.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.860
- And he was presenting Ismail.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.019
And so we had this
incredible seat behind Oprah.

00:00:44.019 --> 00:00:44.852
(audience cheers)
- Oh.

00:00:44.852 --> 00:00:49.140
- Baby, baby. I left
my body. It was crazy.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.040
She came out.
(Terry laughs)

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.645
I've never seen a white
jumpsuit that white in my life.

00:00:52.645 --> 00:00:53.478
(audience cheers)
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:53.478 --> 00:00:55.830
Right there. Ay, right there.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.357
That's it.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.610
- Oh, y'all were at the tables behind.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.780
- We were at the table behind, yes.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.830
That's me contained.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.210
I was freaking out on the inside.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.650
That's me really trying to be cute.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:05.640
But that white, look at that white.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:06.990
You ain't never seen
white like that, have you?

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.790
- [Kelly] First of all,
she like exudes special.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:09.804
- That's a good look.

00:01:09.804 --> 00:01:10.637
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.470
- Hey, is that a pink watch, sir?

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.303
Is that a pink watch?

00:01:12.303 --> 00:01:13.136
- Yes. I'm actually wearing it right now.

00:01:13.136 --> 00:01:13.969
- Oh man, that's a good looking watch.

00:01:13.969 --> 00:01:15.372
- Yeah, it's by this
Black-owned company called

00:01:15.372 --> 00:01:16.260
Springbreak Watches.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:17.093
- Yeah, that's nice. Nice.

00:01:17.093 --> 00:01:18.211
- [Kelly] All right.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.170
(audience cheers)

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.730
Here's what I was nervous about.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.710
So I'd never done the
Emmy's, and I walk out

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.480
and then I was like, oh no.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.610
Like I had just come from like
a big, huge shoot that day.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.860
It was like, I came straight
from there, from another job

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.540
there, and I didn't know

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.010
all the tables were gonna be behind.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.440
And I was like, wait, I made
sure the front looked good

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.161
but I dunno what the back looks like.

00:01:36.161 --> 00:01:38.017
(audience laughs)
I was like,

00:01:38.017 --> 00:01:40.137
"Oh, that's a whole lotta ass."

00:01:40.137 --> 00:01:41.722
(Brandon laughs)

00:01:41.722 --> 00:01:42.555
- You looked fabulous.

00:01:42.555 --> 00:01:44.370
- I was like, well I don't know.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.642
But I definitely wasn't
gonna be wearing white.

00:01:46.642 --> 00:01:48.012
(Brandon laughs)
(Terry laughs)

00:01:48.012 --> 00:01:49.140
I was like, woo.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.175
She looked beautiful.

00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:51.140
- [Brandon] She looked stunning.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:52.020
Yes.
- So, yeah.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.570
So wait, I wanna talk
about your new memoir

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:55.777
it's called "You Gotta Be You,

00:01:55.777 --> 00:01:57.360
"How to Embrace This Messy Life

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.770
and Step Into Who You Really Are."

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.573
So, tell us about it, and
why you wanted to do it.

00:02:01.573 --> 00:02:03.157
(audience cheers and applauds)
(Terry applauds)

00:02:03.157 --> 00:02:05.730
- You know, I wrote the
book because I'm black,

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.140
I'm queer, I'm non-binary,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.300
and I really wanted to create
a blueprint to self-love.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.190
You know, if you're in any
kind of marginalized group,

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.900
loving yourself is a radical act.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.550
You know, when you see representation

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:15.810
there's not a lot of representation

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.730
for those of us in these
marginalized groups.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.580
And so we are taught
to, how do you survive?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:21.750
How do you thrive in a world

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.220
that doesn't show you your value?

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.673
So I wanted to write my experiences

00:02:24.673 --> 00:02:26.557
and really explore the question,

00:02:26.557 --> 00:02:29.198
"Who would I be if society
never got its hands on me?"

00:02:29.198 --> 00:02:31.530
So there's all these things
about, you gotta do this

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.820
you gotta be this, you gotta wear that,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.550
you gotta act like this.
But what about being you?

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.830
And so this book is really
about how I learned to

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.980
step into myself and be
who I am, as opposed to who

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.871
society said I should be based
off the labels of my agenda.

00:02:43.871 --> 00:02:44.704
(audience cheers and applauds)
(Terry applauds)

00:02:44.704 --> 00:02:46.923
- Yeah. Wow.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.778
I love that.

00:02:49.778 --> 00:02:50.611
- [Brandon] Yes. Thank you.

00:02:50.611 --> 00:02:52.747
- Well you didn't know a damn
thing about the other thing,

00:02:52.747 --> 00:02:53.793
but you knew all about this.
(Brandon laughs)

00:02:53.793 --> 00:02:55.080
- Knew 'bout my book.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:58.110
- Kelly, if you're good with you.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:58.943
- [Brandon] Yes.

00:02:58.943 --> 00:03:00.570
- Isn't that the most important thing?

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.677
- [Brandon] It's the most important thing,

00:03:01.677 --> 00:03:03.090
but it's the hardest thing.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:03.923
- Right.

00:03:03.923 --> 00:03:05.040
- It's the hardest thing
to like, when, again,

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.570
when you're in a world that tells you

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.343
that you're not good
enough because your race--

00:03:08.343 --> 00:03:09.176
- [Kelly] Well and they
tell you what's beautiful

00:03:09.176 --> 00:03:11.280
and they tell you what you should be doing

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.113
and they tell you.

00:03:12.113 --> 00:03:13.230
I feel a lot of us go through that.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.063
- [Brandon] Absolutely.

00:03:14.063 --> 00:03:15.147
- Yeah.

00:03:15.147 --> 00:03:15.980
- I think it's, I mean
I write it from my POV

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:18.300
as Black and queer, but
it's a story for all of us.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.257
It's a universal story.

00:03:19.257 --> 00:03:21.000
Every human wants to love

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.037
and to be loved, to be valued, to be seen.

00:03:23.037 --> 00:03:24.088
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:03:24.088 --> 00:03:24.921
- I agree.

00:03:24.921 --> 00:03:26.670
- And so this story is about shaking

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.744
off what other people have
told you you should do

00:03:28.744 --> 00:03:31.530
and figuring out what's good
for you and what you want.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.560
- I like the idea too, just
shaking off any like, damage

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.393
if you wanna call it,

00:03:35.393 --> 00:03:36.840
or just stuff, baggage,
that's happened in your life.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:37.920
Just shaking that off and like being

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.150
who you really are capable of being.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.491
That's nice.
- Yes.

00:03:40.491 --> 00:03:41.324
Engaging with your trauma.

00:03:41.324 --> 00:03:42.780
I say be messy, you know, like it's messy.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.100
But engage with your trauma

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.500
so that you can actually thrive
with it and move forward.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.333
Because the pieces of our trauma--

00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:48.450
- Instead of repeating it.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.910
- Yes. Because that cycle is real crazy.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:51.750
- [Kelly] Yeah. Vicious.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.240
- Interrupt the pattern.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.600
Interrupt the pattern, yeah.
- Yeah, I agree.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.590
(audience applauding)
- It's not easy to do.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:56.890
No, it's not easy to do.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:58.590
- Well, I'm hoping the book will be one

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:01.770
of the resources people can
use to get on that journey.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.080
- I love reading stuff like
this, even if it's from a point

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:04.980
of view that isn't mine.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:07.290
I think it's interesting
because it's also interesting

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.910
for me to know somebody
else's perspective.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.897
So when you run into different
people, like you're like,

00:04:10.897 --> 00:04:12.090
"Oh, I actually read about this."

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:13.770
Like somebody had this experience

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.870
and you're more understanding.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.400
- Curiosity builds empathy.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.931
If you can engage with other people's--

00:04:18.931 --> 00:04:19.764
- Oh, I am so curious.

00:04:19.764 --> 00:04:20.597
- Yes!

00:04:20.597 --> 00:04:21.430
- To a fault.

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:22.650
- Of course, me too.
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.270
But that's why you got this platform,

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.040
because you are curious
and it builds empathy

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.960
and you're helping
other people get exposed

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.850
to experiences they wouldn't have had.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.020
And now they're building empathy.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.157
So when they do meet someone
like me, they're like,

00:04:33.157 --> 00:04:35.250
"Oh that's a human
being," I'm a human being.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.050
Thus, nothing human can be alien to me.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.820
That's a quote by Terence.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.230
That's what I live my life by.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:41.146
- I love that.

00:04:41.146 --> 00:04:43.685
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:04:43.685 --> 00:04:44.518
- Thank you.

00:04:44.518 --> 00:04:46.260
- So, you're also in the animated series

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.520
Big Mouth on Netflix.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.630
So what's happening?
- Yes.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.180
So this season, season six,
is coming out October 28th

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.395
and we are focused on family.

00:04:52.395 --> 00:04:55.470
Which kind of relates, you
know, all the trauma of family.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.210
So all of our characters
have different things

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.740
that they're reckoning
with in terms of their

00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.573
family.

00:04:59.573 --> 00:05:00.406
- Especially like generational trauma.

00:05:00.406 --> 00:05:01.242
- [Brandon] Hey, come on.

00:05:01.242 --> 00:05:02.075
- Hey.

00:05:02.075 --> 00:05:03.847
- Hey.
(Brandon laughs)

00:05:03.847 --> 00:05:06.180
- Hey. Hey. We need another break.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.800
Brandon's book, "You Gotta Be You"

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.603
is out now, y'all have to go get it.

